permitted (approved travelling wildlife exhibitions only), import permit required, high. Keeping: wildlife, permit required to possess, travelling wildlife exhibition permit required","src":"Requirements for importing and keeping wildlife in Tasmania (2017)","url":"https://nre.tas.gov.au/Documents/Requirements%20for%20importing%20and%20keeping%20wildlife%20in%20Tasmania.pdf","checked":"2026-11-08"},{"level":"ok","label":"Not banned in WA","detail":"Not on WA's noxious or high-risk lists. Bringing it in from interstate needs DPIRD translocation approval. On the national Live Import List (Only albino form of Astyanax jordani).","src":"Importing and keeping live fish (DPIRD)","url":"https://www.dpird.wa.gov.au/businesses/biosecurity/aquatic-biosecurity/importing-and-keeping-live-fish-translocation/","checked":"2026-11-08"},{"level":"ok","label":"Not banned in WA","detail":"Not on WA's noxious or high-risk lists. Bringing it in from interstate needs DPIRD translocation approval. On the national Live Import List (of minimum length 3 cm SL).","src":"Importing and keeping live fish (DPIRD)","url":"https://www.dpird.wa.gov.au/businesses/biosecurity/aquatic-biosecurity/importing-and-keeping-live-fish-translocation/","checked":"2026-11-08"},{"level":"ok","label":"Not banned in WA","detail":"Not on WA's noxious or high-risk lists. Bringing it in from interstate needs DPIRD translocation approval. On the national Live Import List (of minimum length 2.5 cm SL).","src":"Importing and keeping live fish (DPIRD)","url":"https://www.dpird.wa.gov.au/businesses/biosecurity/aquatic-biosecurity/importing-and-keeping-live-fish-translocation/","checked":"2026-11-08"},{"level":"ok","label":"Not banned in WA","detail":"Not on WA's noxious or high-risk lists. Bringing it in from interstate needs DPIRD translocation approval. On the national Live Import List (of minimum length 5 cm SL).","src":"Importing and keeping live fish (DPIRD)","url":"https://www.dpird.wa.gov.au/businesses/biosecurity/aquatic-biosecurity/importing-and-keeping-live-fish-translocation/","checked":"2026-11-08"},{"level":"ok","label":"Not banned in WA","detail":"Not on WA's noxious or high-risk lists. Bringing it in from interstate needs DPIRD translocation approval. On the national Live Import List (Only male Bagrichthys hypselopterus).","src":"Importing and keeping live fish (DPIRD)","url":"https://www.dpird.wa.gov.au/businesses/biosecurity/aquatic-biosecurity/importing-and-keeping-live-fish-translocation/","checked":"2026-11-08"}],"guide":[{"n":"Goldfish","sci":"Carassius auratus","fam":"Cyprinidae","size":"10-30 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful, messy eaters.","setup":"Big filtered tank or pond, cool water, no heater.","note":"Fancy varieties need warmer, gentler water than common goldfish.","flags":"r","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/carassius-auratus.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gold_fish1.jpg"}},{"n":"Koi","sci":"Cyprinus carpio","fam":"Cyprinidae","size":"60-90 cm","care":2,"temp":"Peaceful, very long lived.","setup":"Large deep pond with strong filtration.","note":"Never release: wild carp are a serious pest. The Koi Society of WA rehomes unwanted koi.","flags":"r","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":1,"QLD":2},"photo":{"f":"img/cyprinus-carpio.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cyprinus_carpio_2008_G1_%28cropped%29.jpg"}},{"n":"Guppy","sci":"Poecilia reticulata","fam":"Poeciliidae","size":"3-6 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful and lively.","setup":"Small heated tank with plants.","note":"Breeds constantly. Hundreds of colour and tail forms.","flags":"r,x","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":3},"photo":{"f":"img/poecilia-reticulata.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guppy_pho_0048.jpg"}},{"n":"Platy","sci":"Xiphophorus maculatus","fam":"Poeciliidae","size":"4-6 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful.","setup":"Heated community tank.","note":"Hardy livebearer, good first fish.","flags":"r,x","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/xiphophorus-maculatus.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rainbow_wag_platy.jpg"}},{"n":"Swordtail","sci":"Xiphophorus hellerii","fam":"Poeciliidae","size":"10-14 cm","care":1,"temp":"Mostly peaceful; males spar.","setup":"Heated tank with swimming room.","note":"Males carry the long 'sword' on the tail.","flags":"r,x","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/xiphophorus-hellerii.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DSC_0690_-_Edited.jpg"}},{"n":"Pygmy swordtail","sci":"Xiphophorus pygmaeus","fam":"Poeciliidae","size":"3-4 cm","care":2,"temp":"Peaceful.","setup":"Heated planted tank.","note":"Listed as high risk in WA even though its larger relatives are common.","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":4},"photo":{"f":"img/xiphophorus-pygmaeus.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pygmy_Swordtail.jpg"}},{"n":"Siamese fighting fish","sci":"Betta splendens","fam":"Osphronemidae","size":"6-7 cm","care":1,"temp":"Males fight each other.","setup":"Heated, filtered tank of 20 L or more, gentle flow.","note":"Keep one male per tank.","flags":"r,x","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/betta-splendens.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HM_Orange_M_Sarawut.jpg"}},{"n":"Neon tetra","sci":"Paracheirodon innesi","fam":"Characidae","size":"3-4 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful schooling fish.","setup":"Heated planted tank, keep 8 or more.","note":"Classic community fish.","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/paracheirodon-innesi.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Neonsalmler_Paracheirodon_innesi.jpg"}},{"n":"Cardinal tetra","sci":"Paracheirodon axelrodi","fam":"Characidae","size":"4-5 cm","care":2,"temp":"Peaceful schooling fish.","setup":"Warm, soft water, planted tank.","note":"Like a neon but the red runs the whole body.","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/paracheirodon-axelrodi.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cardinal_Paracheirodon_axelrodi_%283%29.jpg"}},{"n":"Zebra danio","sci":"Danio rerio","fam":"Danionidae","size":"4-5 cm","care":1,"temp":"Active and peaceful.","setup":"Room or mild heat, swimming space.","note":"Very hardy. Long-fin and colour forms exist.","flags":"r","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/danio-rerio.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zebrafisch.jpg"}},{"n":"White cloud mountain minnow","sci":"Tanichthys albonubes","fam":"Danionidae","size":"3-4 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful schooling fish.","setup":"Unheated tank is fine.","note":"Good cool-water community fish.","flags":"r","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/tanichthys-albonubes.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:White_Cloud_Mountain_Minnow_1.jpg"}},{"n":"Harlequin rasbora","sci":"Trigonostigma heteromorpha","fam":"Danionidae","size":"4-5 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful schooling fish.","setup":"Heated planted tank.","note":"Easy, calm schooling fish.","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/trigonostigma-heteromorpha.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Harlequin_rasboras_03.jpg"}},{"n":"Dwarf gourami","sci":"Trichogaster lalius","fam":"Osphronemidae","size":"6-8 cm","care":2,"temp":"Peaceful but shy.","setup":"Heated planted tank with floating plants.","note":"Males are brightly coloured; females are silver-grey.","flags":"r,x","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/trichogaster-lalius.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Colisa_lalia-Male_and_Female.jpg"}},{"n":"Pearl gourami","sci":"Trichopodus leerii","fam":"Osphronemidae","size":"10-12 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful.","setup":"Heated planted tank.","note":"Males get a deep orange throat.","flags":"x","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/trichopodus-leerii.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trichopodus_leerii_Natural_History_Museum_University_of_Pisa.jpg"}},{"n":"Bronze corydoras","sci":"Corydoras aeneus","fam":"Callichthyidae","size":"6-7 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful bottom dweller.","setup":"Soft sand, groups of 5 or more.","note":"Cleans up leftovers but still needs its own food.","flags":"r","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/corydoras-aeneus.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Corydoras_aeneus_2.jpg"}},{"n":"Bristlenose catfish","sci":"Ancistrus cirrhosus","fam":"Loricariidae","size":"10-13 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful algae eater.","setup":"Heated tank with driftwood to rasp.","note":"Only Australian-bred stock: not on the national import list.","flags":"r,x","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":1},"photo":{"f":"img/ancistrus-cirrhosus.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancistrus_cirrhosus.jpg"}},{"n":"Angelfish","sci":"Pterophyllum scalare","fam":"Cichlidae","size":"15 cm long, 20 cm tall","care":2,"temp":"Semi-peaceful; will eat small fish.","setup":"Tall heated tank.","note":"Many colour forms.","flags":"r","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/pterophyllum-scalare.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pterophyllum_scalare_Natural_History_Museum_University_of_Pisa.jpg"}},{"n":"Discus","sci":"Symphysodon aequifasciatus","fam":"Cichlidae","size":"15-20 cm","care":3,"temp":"Peaceful, sensitive.","setup":"Warm (28-30°C), very clean soft water.","note":"Demanding: frequent big water changes.","flags":"r","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/symphysodon-aequifasciatus.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%9D%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B5%D0%B2%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%B7%D0%BE%D0%BE%D0%BF%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BA._%D0%90%D0%BA%D0%B2%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%83%D0%BC.8_-_panoramio.jpg"}},{"n":"Oscar","sci":"Astronotus ocellatus","fam":"Cichlidae","size":"30-35 cm","care":2,"temp":"Bold, eats anything that fits.","setup":"Very large heated tank, strong filter.","note":"Recognises its owner. Gets big fast.","flags":"r","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/astronotus-ocellatus.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Astronotus_ocellatus.jpg"}},{"n":"Kribensis","sci":"Pelvicachromis pulcher","fam":"Cichlidae","size":"7-10 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful except when breeding.","setup":"Heated tank with caves.","note":"Pairs guard their fry together.","flags":"x","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/pelvicachromis-pulcher.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:P_pulcher_male_female.jpg"}},{"n":"German blue ram","sci":"Mikrogeophagus ramirezi","fam":"Cichlidae","size":"5-7 cm","care":3,"temp":"Peaceful dwarf cichlid.","setup":"Warm, soft, very clean water.","note":"Beautiful but delicate.","flags":"r","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/mikrogeophagus-ramirezi.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mikrogeophagus_ramirezi_male.jpg"}},{"n":"Clown loach","sci":"Chromobotia macracanthus","fam":"Botiidae","size":"20-30 cm","care":2,"temp":"Social and playful.","setup":"Large heated tank, groups of 5 or more, hiding spots.","note":"Sold small but grows large and lives 20+ years.","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/chromobotia-macracanthus.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chromobotia_macracanthus.jpg"}},{"n":"Kuhli loach","sci":"Pangio kuhlii","fam":"Cobitidae","size":"8-10 cm","care":2,"temp":"Shy, nocturnal.","setup":"Soft sand, plenty of cover, groups.","note":"Eel-like burrower.","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0}},{"n":"Oriental weather loach","sci":"Misgurnus anguillicaudatus","fam":"Cobitidae","size":"15-25 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful.","setup":"Cool tank with soft sand.","note":"Popular in other states but noxious in WA.","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":5,"QLD":2},"photo":{"f":"img/misgurnus-anguillicaudatus.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Misgurnus_anguillicaudatus.jpg"}},{"n":"Tiger barb","sci":"Puntigrus tetrazona","fam":"Cyprinidae","size":"6-7 cm","care":1,"temp":"Fin-nippers; keep 6 or more.","setup":"Heated tank, no long-finned tank mates.","note":"Green and albino forms are common.","flags":"r","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/puntigrus-tetrazona.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tiger_barb_fish.jpg"}},{"n":"Tinfoil barb","sci":"Barbonymus schwanenfeldii","fam":"Cyprinidae","size":"30-35 cm","care":2,"temp":"Peaceful but huge.","setup":"Very large tank.","note":"On WA's high-risk list.","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":6},"photo":{"f":"img/barbonymus-schwanenfeldii.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barbonymus_schwanefeldii_Natural_History_Museum_University_of_Pisa.jpg"}},{"n":"Siamese algae eater","sci":"Crossocheilus oblongus","fam":"Cyprinidae","size":"12-15 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful, active.","setup":"Heated planted tank.","note":"One of the few fish that eats black beard algae.","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/crossocheilus-oblongus.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crossocheilus_siamensis_by_Ark.jpg"}},{"n":"Red-bellied piranha","sci":"Pygocentrus nattereri","fam":"Serrasalmidae","size":"25-30 cm","care":2,"temp":"Skittish group predator.","setup":"Large heated tank.","note":"Piranhas are on WA's high-risk list.","flags":"d","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":7},"photo":{"f":"img/pygocentrus-nattereri.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pygocentrus_nattereri_-_Karlsruhe_Zoo_01.jpg"}},{"n":"Silver arowana","sci":"Osteoglossum bicirrhosum","fam":"Osteoglossidae","size":"90 cm+","care":3,"temp":"Predatory jumper.","setup":"Huge covered tank.","note":"On WA's high-risk list.","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":8},"photo":{"f":"img/osteoglossum-bicirrhosum.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Osteoglossum_bicirrhosum.JPG"}},{"n":"Eastern mosquitofish (gambusia)","sci":"Gambusia holbrooki","fam":"Poeciliidae","size":"3-6 cm","care":1,"temp":"Aggressive fin-nipper.","setup":"Not allowed.","note":"A major pest of WA waterways. Noxious: don't keep or move it.","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":9,"QLD":2},"photo":{"f":"img/gambusia-holbrooki.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:EasternMosquitoFishJG_Female.jpg"}},{"n":"Mozambique tilapia","sci":"Oreochromis mossambicus","fam":"Cichlidae","size":"30-40 cm","care":1,"temp":"Aggressive.","setup":"Not allowed.","note":"Established pest in parts of WA. Noxious.","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":10,"QLD":2},"photo":{"f":"img/oreochromis-mossambicus.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oreochromis_mossambicus.JPG"}},{"n":"Western pygmy perch","sci":"Nannoperca vittata","fam":"Percichthyidae","size":"5-8 cm","care":2,"temp":"Peaceful, a bit shy.","setup":"Cool planted tank, no heater.","note":"South-west WA native. A great small native for an unheated tank.","flags":"x","sub":"native","st":{"WA":11},"photo":{"f":"img/nannoperca-vittata.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Western_Pygmy_Perch_Map_.jpg"}},{"n":"Western minnow","sci":"Galaxias occidentalis","fam":"Galaxiidae","size":"10-15 cm","care":2,"temp":"Active schooling fish.","setup":"Cool, well-oxygenated water with flow.","note":"South-west WA native.","sub":"native","st":{"WA":11},"photo":{"f":"img/galaxias-occidentalis.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Galaxias_occidentalis_%28Western_galaxias%29_001.jpg"}},{"n":"Black-stripe minnow","sci":"Galaxiella nigrostriata","fam":"Galaxiidae","size":"4 cm","care":3,"temp":"Peaceful, tiny.","setup":"Soft, acidic, cool water.","note":"Threatened south-west native. Seasonal wetland specialist.","flags":"t","sub":"native","st":{"WA":11},"photo":{"f":"img/galaxiella-nigrostriata.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Galaxiella_nigrostriata.jpg"}},{"n":"Spangled perch","sci":"Leiopotherapon unicolor","fam":"Terapontidae","size":"20-30 cm","care":1,"temp":"Aggressive, eats small fish.","setup":"Large tank, keep with robust fish only.","note":"Found across most of WA.","sub":"native","st":{"WA":11},"photo":{"f":"img/leiopotherapon-unicolor.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FMIB_36092_Therapon_unicclor.jpeg"}},{"n":"Western rainbowfish","sci":"Melanotaenia australis","fam":"Melanotaeniidae","size":"8-10 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful schooling fish.","setup":"Heated or warm tank, swimming room.","note":"Kimberley and Pilbara native.","flags":"r,x","sub":"native","st":{"WA":11},"photo":{"f":"img/melanotaenia-australis.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:300_Melanotaenia_australis_Western_rainbowfish_Mitchell_River_NP_VIII-2013.jpg"}},{"n":"South-west freshwater cobbler","sci":"Tandanus bostocki","fam":"Plotosidae","size":"30-40 cm","care":2,"temp":"Peaceful, nocturnal.","setup":"Large cool tank with hides.","note":"Has venomous spines: handle with care.","flags":"d","sub":"native","st":{"WA":11}},{"n":"Barramundi","sci":"Lates calcarifer","fam":"Latidae","size":"1 m+","care":3,"temp":"Large predator.","setup":"Huge tank or pond.","note":"Northern WA native. Sold as fingerlings but outgrows home tanks.","sub":"native","st":{"WA":11},"photo":{"f":"img/lates-calcarifer.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lates_calcarifer%2C_2014-09-19a.jpg"}},{"n":"Eastern rainbowfish","sci":"Melanotaenia splendida","fam":"Melanotaeniidae","size":"10-12 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful schooling fish.","setup":"Warm tank, swimming room.","note":"An Australian native but not a WA one: needs approval to bring into WA.","flags":"x","sub":"native","st":{"WA":1},"photo":{"f":"img/melanotaenia-splendida.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eastern_Rainbowfish_01.jpg"}},{"n":"Pacific blue-eye","sci":"Pseudomugil signifer","fam":"Pseudomugilidae","size":"4-6 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful.","setup":"Planted tank.","note":"East-coast native.","flags":"x","sub":"native","st":{"WA":1},"photo":{"f":"img/pseudomugil-signifer.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:052fishcropped.jpg"}},{"n":"Murray cod","sci":"Maccullochella peelii","fam":"Percichthyidae","size":"1 m+","care":3,"temp":"Huge predator.","setup":"Pond or very large tank.","note":"Not a WA native: DPIRD lists it as non-endemic.","sub":"native","st":{"WA":1},"photo":{"f":"img/maccullochella-peelii.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Murray_cod02_melb_aquarium.jpg"}},{"n":"Silver perch","sci":"Bidyanus bidyanus","fam":"Terapontidae","size":"30-40 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful, schooling.","setup":"Pond or big tank.","note":"Not a WA native: DPIRD lists it as non-endemic.","sub":"native","st":{"WA":1},"photo":{"f":"img/bidyanus-bidyanus.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bidyanus_bidyanus_as_depicted_by_Fishing_and_Aquaculture%2C_Department_of_Primary_Industries%2C_New_South_Wales.jpg"}},{"n":"Ocellaris clownfish","sci":"Amphiprion ocellaris","fam":"Pomacentridae","size":"8-11 cm","care":2,"temp":"Hardy, can be territorial.","setup":"Reef tank, anemone optional.","note":"Captive-bred fish are easy and widely available.","flags":"r","sub":"marine","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/amphiprion-ocellaris.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clown_fish_in_the_Andaman_Coral_Reef.jpg"}},{"n":"Blue tang","sci":"Paracanthurus hepatus","fam":"Acanthuridae","size":"25-30 cm","care":3,"temp":"Active swimmer.","setup":"Large marine tank with lots of open water.","note":"Prone to white spot. Needs a big tank.","sub":"marine","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/paracanthurus-hepatus.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paletten-Doktorfisch_M%C3%BCnster.JPG"}},{"n":"Yellow tang","sci":"Zebrasoma flavescens","fam":"Acanthuridae","size":"18-20 cm","care":2,"temp":"Can bully other tangs.","setup":"Large reef tank with algae to graze.","note":"Grazes algae constantly.","sub":"marine","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/zebrasoma-flavescens.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zebrasoma_flavescens_Luc_Viatour.jpg"}},{"n":"Royal gramma","sci":"Gramma loreto","fam":"Grammatidae","size":"8 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful, hides in rockwork.","setup":"Reef tank with caves.","note":"Hardy, colourful beginner marine fish.","sub":"marine","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/gramma-loreto.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gramma_loreto%2C_Adult_%28Royal_Gramma%29.jpg"}},{"n":"Mandarin dragonet","sci":"Synchiropus splendidus","fam":"Callionymidae","size":"6-7 cm","care":3,"temp":"Peaceful, slow feeder.","setup":"Mature reef tank full of live copepods.","note":"Often starves in new tanks.","flags":"x","sub":"marine","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/synchiropus-splendidus.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Synchiropus_splendidus_2_Luc_Viatour.jpg"}},{"n":"Banggai cardinalfish","sci":"Pterapogon kauderni","fam":"Apogonidae","size":"7-8 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful, slow.","setup":"Reef tank.","note":"Choose captive-bred: wild stocks are endangered.","sub":"marine","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/pterapogon-kauderni.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banggai_cardinalfish_%28Pterapogon_kauderni%29_%2843875107345%29.jpg"}},{"n":"Red lionfish","sci":"Pterois volitans","fam":"Scorpaenidae","size":"30-38 cm","care":2,"temp":"Predator, eats small fish.","setup":"Large marine tank.","note":"Venomous spines: very painful sting.","flags":"d","sub":"marine","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/pterois-volitans.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pterois_volitans_Manado-e_edit.jpg"}},{"n":"Six-line wrasse","sci":"Pseudocheilinus hexataenia","fam":"Labridae","size":"7-8 cm","care":1,"temp":"Busy; can pester small fish.","setup":"Reef tank with rock.","note":"Eats pest flatworms and bristleworms.","sub":"marine","st":{"WA":12},"photo":{"f":"img/pseudocheilinus-hexataenia.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Six_Line_Wrasse_-_Pseudocheilinus_hexataenia_%28cropped%29.jpg"}},{"n":"Marron","sci":"Cherax cainii","fam":"Parastacidae","size":"Up to 38 cm","care":2,"temp":"Will eat tank mates.","setup":"Cool, well-oxygenated tank or pond with hides.","note":"WA's iconic freshwater crayfish. Catching wild marron needs a licence and is seasonal.","flags":"r","sub":"crust","st":{"WA":11},"photo":{"f":"img/cherax-cainii.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cherax_cainii.jpg"}},{"n":"Gilgie","sci":"Cherax quinquecarinatus","fam":"Parastacidae","size":"Up to 10 cm","care":1,"temp":"Hardy.","setup":"Cool tank with hides.","note":"Small south-west WA crayfish.","sub":"crust","st":{"WA":11}},{"n":"Koonac","sci":"Cherax preissii","fam":"Parastacidae","size":"Up to 15 cm","care":1,"temp":"Burrower.","setup":"Cool tank with deep substrate and hides.","note":"South-west WA native.","sub":"crust","st":{"WA":11},"photo":{"f":"img/cherax-preissii.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cheraxpreissi.jpeg"}},{"n":"Yabby","sci":"Cherax destructor","fam":"Parastacidae","size":"Up to 20 cm","care":1,"temp":"Will eat tank mates.","setup":"Tank or pond with hides.","note":"Not a WA native: established here and competes with marron.","flags":"r","sub":"crust","st":{"WA":13},"photo":{"f":"img/cherax-destructor.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cherax_destructor_%28Cyan_yabby%29.jpg"}},{"n":"Redclaw","sci":"Cherax quadricarinatus","fam":"Parastacidae","size":"Up to 25 cm","care":1,"temp":"Will eat tank mates.","setup":"Warm tank with hides.","note":"Not a WA native. Feral in the Ord River.","flags":"x","sub":"crust","st":{"WA":13},"photo":{"f":"img/cherax-quadricarinatus.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cherax_quadricarinatus_im_Aquarium.jpg"}},{"n":"Red swamp crayfish","sci":"Procambarus clarkii","fam":"Cambaridae","size":"Up to 15 cm","care":1,"temp":"Aggressive.","setup":"Not allowed.","note":"A serious invasive pest overseas. Noxious in WA.","sub":"crust","st":{"WA":14},"photo":{"f":"img/procambarus-clarkii.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Procambarus_clarkii.jpg"}},{"n":"Marbled crayfish","sci":"Procambarus virginalis","fam":"Cambaridae","size":"10-13 cm","care":1,"temp":"Clones itself: every one is female.","setup":"Not allowed.","note":"One escapee can start a whole population. Covered by the noxious listing for Procambarus fallax.","sub":"crust","st":{"WA":15},"photo":{"f":"img/procambarus-virginalis.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Procambarus_fallax_forma_virginalis.jpg"}},{"n":"Cherry shrimp","sci":"Neocaridina davidi","fam":"Atyidae","size":"2-3 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful.","setup":"Small planted tank.","note":"Very popular in other states. Many colour forms.","flags":"r,x","sub":"crust","st":{"WA":13},"photo":{"f":"img/neocaridina-davidi.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_Cherry_Shrimp_1.jpg"}},{"n":"Amano shrimp","sci":"Caridina multidentata","fam":"Atyidae","size":"4-5 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful algae eater.","setup":"Planted tank.","note":"Larvae need salt water, so they rarely breed in tanks.","sub":"crust","st":{"WA":13},"photo":{"f":"img/caridina-multidentata.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amano_Garnele_%2885281493%29.jpeg"}},{"n":"Mystery snail","sci":"Pomacea diffusa","fam":"Ampullariidae","size":"5 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful.","setup":"Heated tank with a lid.","note":"Apple snails are a big agricultural pest risk.","flags":"r","sub":"other","st":{"WA":13},"photo":{"f":"img/pomacea-diffusa.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pomacea_diffusa_01.JPG"}},{"n":"Nerite snail","sci":"Neritina natalensis","fam":"Neritidae","size":"2-3 cm","care":1,"temp":"Peaceful algae eater.","setup":"Any tank.","note":"Won't breed in fresh water.","flags":"r","sub":"other","st":{"WA":13},"photo":{"f":"img/neritina-natalensis.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Naturalis_Biodiversity_Center_-_RMNH.MOL.151741_-_Vittina_natalensis_%28Reeve%2C_1855%29_-_Neritidae_-_Mollusc_shell.jpeg"}},{"n":"Axolotl","sci":"Ambystoma mexicanum","fam":"Ambystomatidae","size":"20-25 cm","care":2,"temp":"Calm.","setup":"Cool (under 20°C) tank, fine sand or bare floor.","note":"An amphibian, so the WA Organism List covers it rather than the fish lists.","flags":"r","sub":"other","st":{"WA":16,"TAS":17},"photo":{"f":"img/ambystoma-mexicanum.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Axolotl_ganz.jpg"}},{"n":"Abramites hypselonotus","sci":"Abramites hypselonotus","note":"Abramites hypselonotus – known as the marbled headstander or the high-backed headstander – is a member of the family Anostomidae of the order Characiformes. Under normal fish classifying rules, the marbled headstander would be classified as a surface dweller.","w":"Abramites hypselonotus","auto":"2026-11-09","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/abramites-hypselonotus.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abramites_hypselonotus.jpg"}},{"n":"Arnoldichthys","sci":"Arnoldichthys spilopterus","note":"Arnoldichthys is monospecific genus of freshwater ray-finned fish in the family Lepidarchidae. The only species in the genus is Arnoldichthys spilopterus, the Niger tetra.","w":"Arnoldichthys","auto":"2026-11-08","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/arnoldichthys-spilopterus.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arnoldichthys_spilopterus.JPG"}},{"n":"Astyanax jordani","sci":"Astyanax jordani","note":"Astyanax jordani is a species of freshwater ray-finned fish belonging to the family Acestrorhamphidae, the American characins. This fish is found in Mexico. It is known in the aquarium trade as the blind cave tetra, or by its local Spanish name sardina ciega.","w":"Astyanax jordani","auto":"2026-11-08","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":18},"photo":{"f":"img/astyanax-jordani.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Astyanax_jordani_T%C3%A9tra_aveugle_Aquarium_Li%C3%A8ge_30012016_01.jpg"}},{"n":"Black ghost knifefish","sci":"Apteronotus albifrons","note":"The black ghost knifefish is a tropical ornamental fish belonging to the ghost knifefish family (Apteronotidae). They originate in freshwater habitats in South America where they range from Venezuela to the Paraguay–Paraná River, including the Amazon Basin. They are popular in aquaria.","w":"Black ghost knifefish","auto":"2026-11-08","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/apteronotus-albifrons.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Black_Ghost_Knifefish_400.jpg"}},{"n":"Blue acara","sci":"Andinoacara pulcher","note":"The Blue Acara is a species of cichlid, from the family Cichlidae and order Cichliformes, that has a bright blue-grey coloration throughout the scales across its body. Andinoacaara pulcher is a freshwater species found naturally in Trinidad and Venezuela but is also found and sold for aquariums.","w":"Blue acara","auto":"2026-11-08","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":19},"photo":{"f":"img/andinoacara-pulcher.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aequidens_pulcher.jpg"}},{"n":"Brown ghost knifefish","sci":"Apteronotus leptorhynchus","note":"The brown ghost knifefish is a species of weakly electric knifefish in the family Apteronotidae. The brown ghost knifefish is the only vertebrate proven to have negligible brain aging thus far. As such, they are extensively researched as a model species for neurological and developmental studies. In the wild, A.","w":"Brown ghost knifefish","auto":"2026-11-08","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/apteronotus-leptorhynchus.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brownghostknifefish.jpg"}},{"n":"Clown barb","sci":"Barbodes everetti","note":"Barbodes everetti, the clown barb or Everett's barb is a species of cyprinid fish native to Borneo and Sumatra. It inhabits clear streams in forested foothills and can also be found in forest floor puddles as shallow as 15 centimetres (5.9 in) or less.","w":"Clown barb","auto":"2026-11-09","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/barbodes-everetti.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clownbarbe_2.jpg"}},{"n":"Dwarf loach","sci":"Ambastaia sidthimunki","note":"The dwarf loach, ladderback loach, pygmy loach, chain loach or chain botia is a freshwater fish belonging to the family Botiidae. Formerly included in the genus Yasuhikotakia, it is frequently seen in the aquarium trade, the product of captive breeding.","w":"Dwarf loach","auto":"2026-11-08","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":20},"photo":{"f":"img/ambastaia-sidthimunki.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yasuhikotakia_sidthimunki.jpg"}},{"n":"Emperor cichlid","sci":"Aulonocara nyassae","note":"Aulonocara nyassae, known as the emperor cichlid, is a species of haplochromine Cichlid that is endemic to Lake Malawi in Africa. It has been recorded from the southeastern arm of the lake and may be present in the southwestern arm.","w":"Aulonocara nyassae","auto":"2026-11-08","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":21},"photo":{"f":"img/aulonocara-nyassae.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aulonocara_nyassae.JPG"}},{"n":"Emperor lancer catfish","sci":"Bagrichthys hypselopterus","note":"Bagrichthys hypselopterus, the Emperor lancer catfish or black lancer catfish, is a species of freshwater ray-finned fish belonging to the family Bagridae, the naked or bagrid catfishes. This catfish is endemic to Indonesia where it is an important food fish.","w":"Bagrichthys hypselopterus","auto":"2026-11-08","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":22},"photo":{"f":"img/bagrichthys-hypselopterus.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bagrichthys_hypselopterus.jpg"}},{"n":"Pseudoambassis macleayi","sci":"Ambassis macleayi","note":"Pseudoambassis macleayi, commonly known as Macleay's glassfish, Macleay's glass perchlet, Macleay's perchlet, reticulated glassfish, reticulated perchlet, or network perchlet, is a species of freshwater fish in the family Ambassidae. It is native to northern Australia and the trans-Fly River region of New Guinea.","w":"Pseudoambassis macleayi","auto":"2026-11-08","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/ambassis-macleayi.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Glassfish_Ambassis.jpg"}},{"n":"Scalloped glassfish","sci":"Ambassis nalua","note":"Ambassis nalua, the scalloped glassfish or scalloped perchlet, is a species of ray-finned fish in the genus Ambassis. It is native to the Indo-Pacific region, form India to Australia and New Guinea, where it occurs in bays, estuaries and mangrove-lined creeks.","w":"Ambassis nalua","auto":"2026-11-08","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/ambassis-nalua.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ambassis_nalua_%28Hamilton%2C_1822%29.jpg"}},{"n":"Yellow-tailed African tetra","sci":"Alestopetersius caudalis","note":"The yellow-tailed African tetra is a species of freshwater ray-finned fish belonging to the African tetra family Alestidae. This species is found in the Congo River basin, in both the DRC and the Republic of the Congo.","w":"Yellow-tailed African tetra","auto":"2026-11-09","sub":"fresh","st":{"WA":0},"photo":{"f":"img/alestopetersius-caudalis.jpg","c":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yellow_tailed_tetra.jpg"}}]}